<title>CHINA: China cuts finished palm oil import duty to 12 pct.</title>
<headline>China cuts finished palm oil import duty to 12 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>China cut the import duty on finished palm oil to 12 percent, effective January 1, an official of the customs administration under the State Council, or cabinet, said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>He declined to give the previous import duty level.</p>
<p>However, an official of the China National Cereals, Oils and Foodstuffs Import and Export Corp said the previous import duty on finished palm oil was 18 percent.</p>
<p>The import duty on semi-finished palm oil had been cut to 9.0 percent, the customs administration official said in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>The duty on non-quota imports remained unchanged at 30 percent, he said.</p>
</text>
